# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Project Workspace

> Generated {{RENDER_DATE}} from harness kit {{KIT_VERSION}}. This tree is Layer C (project workspace). The harness itself never lives here.

## Structure & ownership

| Path | Purpose | Writing role |
|---|---|---|
| `00-context/` | brief, scope, stakeholders + RACI, metrics, glossary, business rules, constraints, RAID | BA drafts; PM ratifies |
| `01-requirements/` | BRD/PRD, stories, acceptance criteria, NFRs, issue drafts, change requests | BA |
| `02-design/` | UX strategy, IA, journeys, screens, design system, accessibility, handoff, audits | Designer |
| `03-architecture/` | architecture, data model, contracts, integrations, environments, spikes, `adr/` | Developer |
| `04-quality/` | test strategy, plans, cases, reports, defects, review copies | QA |
| `05-security/` | threat model, baseline, reviews, remediation log, incidents | Security Monitor |
| `06-operations/` | deployment, backup/restore, runbooks, smoke tests, release notes | PM/Developer |
| `knowledge/` | atomized cited knowledge base (`README` = rules) | BA via staging workflow |
| `decisions/decision-register.md` | append-only owner decisions | PM records; owner approves |
| `status/` | phase state, blockers, metrics, gates, retrospectives | PM |
| `working/<agent>/` | non-authoritative working memory and inbox | each agent |
| `traceability.md` | requirement → story → AC → issue → PR → test → QA | roles write; PM reconciles |

## Reading order

`../../project.yaml` → `../../AGENTS.md` → `status/phase-state.md` → the issue → this area's approved artifacts.

## Rules

1. Every artifact carries the common header (source, status, assumptions, dependencies, open questions, evidence) — see `templates/artifact-templates.md`.
2. Draft ≠ approved. Never present unapproved content as fact.
3. Supersede, never overwrite; the register and KB history survive.
4. `working/` is memory, not knowledge: promote through the correct workflow or delete at retro. Sensitive inbox files stay gitignored.
5. No secrets, no personal data beyond `project.yaml` data policy.
